# Where project/gate/old-words.sh lets an old word through. One entry per line, fields separated by tabs: a path
# glob (`*` within a directory, `**` across), optionally a regular expression (any case) that a line must match
# to pass, and always the reason, starting with #. A glob without a pattern allows the whole file.

# The rename's own record and history, kept as written.
project/archive/**		# written in the earlier vocabulary, each with a header saying so
project/plans/exam-variant-attempt.md		# the plan names the old words it replaces
project/plans/exam-variant-attempt-removal.md		# the work-list names the old words it removes
CHANGELOG.md		# released entries keep the words of their time; the rename's entry carries the name map
project/gate/**		# the gate names the words it looks for

# The user's, pending: not reworded in step 1.
project/todo.md		# loose ends; each section needs a person's judgement
project/plans/agent-neutral-runs.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/jev-judge-research.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/jev-trial.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/onboarding.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/lab.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/lab-report-worked-example.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/oracle-in-proctor.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/setup/**		# the setup wizard's plan and screen mockups; not on the work-list, the user's to reword or archive

# Not proctor's model, or frozen output of an earlier version.
project/learnings/**		# notes on other tools and dated findings, kept as written (the work-list keeps them)
project/lab/**		# throwaway trials over the frozen datasets, which keep the old layout
bench/**		# the judge bench: its own proctor root at an earlier version, unrelated to the rename
docs/reports/**		# published reports, rendered by an earlier version
Proctor.Tests/fixtures/**		# captured transcripts and trajectories, as the agents wrote them

# Batch, gated since the bank (project/plans/bank.md).
project/plans/bank.md		# the plan names the word it removes
project/migrate/**		# the script that moves the earlier layout names its files
project/brief.md		# the founding brief, in the words of its time; the user's to reword
project/plans/report-structure.md		# the report's plan predates the bank; the report is not redrawn yet
exams/exam-authoring/**		# shows agents proctor's docs pinned at an earlier revision, and reads that proctor's layout; waits on todo "Grade the proctor-on-proctor exams with the proctor they were shown"
fixtures/authoring-interrupted/**		# the same exam's fixture
CLAUDE.md	(there is no batch|continue-the-batch)	# saying the word is gone, and that exam's task id
Proctor.Tests/FrictionTests.cs	\["batch"\]	# asserts friction.json no longer carries the key

# The one place an old word is the point.
**	\bno resume verb\b	# D15: after a crash a person or an agent looks for "resume", so the CLI help, docs/cli.md, the skill and exam-authoring say there is none

# Ordinary English or another tool's word.
**	\btest suites?\b	# a project's own tests
**	\btable cells?\b	# a cell of a table
project/plans/on-disk-layout.md	evaluation suite	# the literature's word for an exam, in the words table

# The example reports predate the rename.
README.md	\b(suite|arm|baseline) for (exam|variant|the live variant)\b	# docs/reports/ were rendered in the earlier words; the README maps them for a reader

# eval as evaluation in general, and nb's evals/ directory: not a proctor exam.
**	(?<![A-Za-z])evals/	# nb's own evals/ directory, named in task prompts and comments about nb; a task prompt is in its hash
exams/nb-changes/tasks/far-cause.json	nb's tests and evals all pass	# nb's evals, in a task prompt the task hash covers
CLAUDE.md	reporter of evals	# evaluation in general: what proctor is a runner of
docs/index.html	\ban eval that\b|\bvisibility and evals\b|agent-evals">their write-up	# evaluation in general on the site, and an outside study's URL
skills/proctor-exam/SKILL.md	other eval tools	# evaluation tools in general
project/brief.md	Demystifying evals|where "eval"|evals need to be taken seriously	# evaluation in general, as the brief itself says where "eval" survives
project/plans/on-disk-layout.md	evals literature|\beval run\b	# the literature's words for exam and batch, in the words table
View/**		# the viewer as it moved in on 2026-11-24 (plans/rename-to-auspex.md, stage 1), in the words it was written in; reworded with the rename
project/view/**		# the viewer's design notes, moved in with it; they record what was true when written
bundles/smoke/README.md	smoke eval's bundle	# the bundle's only file: rewording it changes the bundle's identity and so the smoke variant b's hash
project/plans/site.md	"Evals" in the general sense|"eval" was once|evals, measure, grade	# evaluation in general: the site plan says where the word may stand
